{
  "name": "PillAlly in-app palette",
  "version": "1.0",
  "brand": {
    "navy": "#030423",
    "blue": "#2965D2",
    "purple_optional": "#7116D1",
    "note": "Logo colours. Purple #7116D1 may be used as a rare decorative accent only. It fails WCAG 3:1 on navy (2.62:1), so do not use it for text, focus, or taken/missed/due states on dark surfaces. On white it is 7.67:1."
  },
  "css_variable_map": {
    "--bg": "background",
    "--surface": "surface",
    "--elevated": "elevated",
    "--sunk": "sunk",
    "--line": "border",
    "--fg": "primary_text",
    "--muted": "muted_text",
    "--accent": "primary_accent  (fills, borders)",
    "--accent-text": "accent_text  (labels, links; NEW \u2014 required in dark mode)",
    "--accent-ink": "accent_ink",
    "--accent-soft": "accent_soft",
    "--ok": "success",
    "--ok-soft": "success_soft",
    "--warn": "warning",
    "--warn-soft": "warning_soft",
    "--bad": "danger",
    "--bad-soft": "danger_soft",
    "--focus": "focus_ring"
  },
  "implementation_notes": [
    "Keep --accent as #2965D2 for fills and borders in both modes.",
    "Add --accent-text. In light mode it equals #2965D2; in dark mode it must be the lighter #7FA4E6. Logo blue on navy is only 3.72:1 and fails AA for small text (selected tab, Log event, My medicines).",
    "Do not reuse the blue accent as the taken/on-time colour. --ok is a distinct green.",
    "Caregiver no longer needs a separate accent; the app-wide blue already covers that role. Confirm with Frank before dropping the old caregiver override.",
    "Nothing in this folder is approved for the live app until Frank says yes."
  ],
